/-
# Equations in free groups with subgroup constraints (Kourovka Notebook Problem 9.25)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 9.25 (G. S. Makanin): find an algorithm which
recognizes, by an equation `w(x₁, …, xₙ) = 1` in a free group `F` and by a list of finitely
generated subgroups `H₁, …, Hₙ` of `F`, whether there is a solution of this equation satisfying `x₁
∈ H₁, …, xₙ ∈ Hₙ`.
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.FreeGroupEquationsDecidableKourovka1Problem18Wanted

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.ConstrainedEquationsFreeGroupKourovka9Problem25Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 9.25 (G. S.
Makanin). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700558 (`KOU-9.25`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

`F` is the free group `F_k` of finite rank `k`; equations may contain constants. An equation is the
1.18 entry's `Equation k`, a list of letters (generators of `F_k` and unknowns `xᵢ`, with a sign);
each `Hᵢ` is given by a finite list of generating words. Unknowns with index beyond the list of
subgroups are unconstrained, which loses nothing since `F_k` is itself finitely generated. The
algorithm is `ComputablePred` on the `Primcodable` type of (equation, list of generator lists), for
each `k`.
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreeGroupEquationsDecidableKourovka1Problem18Wanted

/-- A word in the free group `F_k = FreeGroup (Fin k)`, read through `FreeGroup.mk`. -/
abbrev Word (k : ℕ) := List (Fin k × Bool)

/-- The equation `w = 1` (`w : Equation k`, from the 1.18 entry) has a solution with `xᵢ ∈ Hᵢ` for
`i < cs.length`, where `Hᵢ` is the subgroup of `F_k` generated by the words in the list `cs[i]`;
unknowns with `i ≥ cs.length` are unconstrained (as if `Hᵢ = F_k`, which is finitely generated). -/
def ConstrainedSolvable {k : ℕ} (w : Equation k) (cs : List (List (Word k))) : Prop :=
  ∃ s : ℕ → FreeGroup (Fin k),
    (∀ (i : ℕ) (hi : i < cs.length), s i ∈ Subgroup.closure {x | ∃ u ∈ cs[i], x = FreeGroup.mk u}) ∧
    FreeGroup.lift (Sum.elim FreeGroup.of s) (FreeGroup.mk w) = 1

/-- Kourovka 9.25 (G. S. Makanin): for every finite rank `k` there is an algorithm deciding, for an
equation `w(x₁, …, xₙ) = 1` (with constants) over the free group `F_k` and finitely generated
subgroups `H₁, …, Hₙ` of `F_k` given by generators, whether the equation has a solution with
`xᵢ ∈ Hᵢ` for all `i`. -/
def constrainedEquationsDecidable : Prop :=
  ∀ k : ℕ, ComputablePred fun p : Equation k × List (List (Word k)) => ConstrainedSolvable p.1 p.2

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive records that such an algorithm is found in
Diekert-Gutiérrez-Hagenah, who prove that the existential theory of equations with rational
constraints in free groups is decidable (PSPACE-complete); constraints `xᵢ ∈ Hᵢ` for finitely
generated subgroups `Hᵢ` are rational constraints. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.),
Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026),
Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 9.25 (G. S. Makanin); resolution: V. Diekert, C. Gutiérrez and
C. Hagenah, The existential theory of equations with rational constraints in free groups is
PSPACE-complete, Inform. and Comput. 202 (2005), no. 2, 105-140, Kourovka Archive of Solved
Problems, Problem 9.25: Such an algorithm is found in Diekert-Gutiérrez-Hagenah,
https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ic.2005.04.002.
-/
public theorem_wanted constrainedEquationsDecidable_holds : constrainedEquationsDecidable

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.ConstrainedEquationsFreeGroupKourovka9Problem25Wanted
